I am producing multiple graphs using facet_wrap and would like to add contextual information (e.g., timestamps, project ID, etc) as annotations on the periphery of the "page".

Here is an example      of what I am currently producing using the following ggplot statements: :

g2  <- ggplot(r_allv) +
           geom_line(aes(x=variable, y=value),linetype=1, color="grey72", size=3, ) +
           geom_line(aes(x=week, y=value, color=factor(id), size=factor(is_profile)),
                       linetype=1)+
           scale_size_manual(values=c(.3,.75),guide=F)+
           scale_color_manual(values=cols,guide=F)+
           labs(title="", x="Weeks", y="Normalized Index")
gg  <- g2+
             facet_wrap(~label,ncol=nc, scales="free_y") +
                        theme(axis.text.x = element_text(size = 5.5)) +
                    ggtitle(paste(main, collapse=" "))
print(gg)
Here is an example of  what I was producing using base R graphics
The following code was used to produce the timestamps on the lower right corner of the "page".  I am interested in achieving comparable results using the ggplot environment.

nr = ceiling(n/nc) # number of rows in plotting layout
op = par(mfrow=c(nr,nc),mar=.5*c(2,3,1,1), oma=c(2,0,3,0), cex.axis=.85,cex.main=1
                        , xaxs="r",xaxt="s",tcl=-.5) # set plotting layout
                :
        (base R graphics statements)
                :
mtext(paste(Sys.time(),"  "),side=1, line=.5, adj=1, outer=T,cex=.6)
        op = par(mfrow=c(1,1))

I appreciate whatever suggestions you can provide.

By the way, this group has provided me with many ideas for improving my visualization efforts as well as solutions to issues that I was having.  Thanks

Alex

