I don't think there is a way to do it in `aes` directly, though a couple options you could do are 1) `ddply` in the `plyr` package, grouping by "Time" and doing the subtraction in each subset or 2) `reshape2` package's `cast` function. That will make the data wide and allow you to subtract. Then you can use `melt` to get it back into long form, which `ggplot2` likes.

